uldenko\\n\\nFollowing his divorce from first wife Judy Langford, Jack Carter married Elizabeth Brasfield, which made him the stepfather of her two children, John Chuldenko and Sarah Chuldenko Reynolds.\\n\\nJohn Chuldenko is a screenwriter and director. He is the creator of the television series \\\"Backseat Drivers\\\" and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.today.com/parents/jimmy-carter-rosalynn-carter-children-grandchildren-rcna101303\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d185\"},\"ref\":\"d185\",\"snippet\":\" ... The establishment of the Emory University Museum (later the Michael C. Carlos Museum of Art) and the High Museum of Art, as well as an art school, further encouraged the growth of the arts in the city. Meanwhile, the older artistic community in Savannah thrived with the expansion ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.georgiaencyclopedia.org/articles/arts-culture/art-in-georgia-from-1895-to-1960/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d186\"},\"ref\":\"d186\",\"snippet\":\" ... The true crime novel follows the infamous mobster Whitey Bulger, the head of the Irish mob in the '70s, and his relationship with childhood friend John Connolly, who grew up to work for the FBI.\\n\\n- Who's starring: Johnny Depp will play Whitey Bulger with Joel Edgerton as ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.popsugar.com/entertainment/books-becoming-movies-2015-36113875\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d151\"},\"ref\":\"d151\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2009, she was cast in the Lifetime TV movie Tribute, as the main character, Cilla. Murphy completed the thriller/drama Abandoned in June 2009 and it was released in 2010, after her death. In November 2009, Murphy left the production of The Caller, which was being filmed ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brittany_Murphy\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d187\"},\"ref\":\"d187\",\"snippet\":\" ... Crews married the former Gladys Barr in 1942 and together they raised two daughters, Peggy Jane and Sally Anne. He is remembered as a God loving, God fearing, and church-going individual of great character and integrity. To this very day he is still revered by those who ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.vdot.virginia.gov/about/workers-memorial/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d152\"},\"ref\":\"d152\",\"snippet\":\" ... Several theories have popped up in the years since the two deaths, with many believing that black mold in the home contributed. There have also been reports of Monjack's controlling behavior, and his and her mother's odd relationship following Murphy's death, leading some to suspect ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goldderby.com/gallery/tragic-deaths-actresses/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d188\"},\"ref\":\"d188\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was at UNO that he found a love and appreciation for poetic form under the direction of poetry professors Kay Murphy and John Gery, Brown said.\\n\\nOne of the features included in his Pulitzer Prize winning book, \\\"The Tradition,\\\" is a form he invented called the duplex ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.uno.edu/news/2020-08-11/pulitzer-prize-poet-and-alumnus-jericho-brown-what-im-doing-now-still-bears-upon-what-i-learned-uno\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d155\"},\"ref\":\"d155\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Murphys are the Garveys' neighbors in Jarden.\\n*Kevin Carroll as John Murphy (seasons 2–3), Erika's husband and head of Jarden's volunteer fire department. He subsequently marries Laurie, and operates as a fraudulent medium.\\n*Jovan Adepo as Michael Murphy (seasons 2–3), Erika and John ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Leftovers_(TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d189\"},\"ref\":\"d189\",\"snippet\":\" ... Unfortunately, sometime between the wedding and Christmas, Daniel Riggs passed away. Daniel lived long enough to see his daughter marry the man who was already the father of Agnes's son John born in January. Agnes and Johnson would go on to have 11 children, and Agnes would ... \",\"title\":\"https://struggleandprogress.com/page/2/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"4c528986ca8e02f94dc958bf4da801eed26b495bd07801de71c821bdfddab9de\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"ab474bb61314db2bb706148f47a017fa8797a893b46c9398830567cab9851d65\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"John Murphy The 100 character Emori relationship married\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d190\"},\"ref\":\"d190\",\"snippet\":\" ... the 2014–2015 television season. The first-season finale was also the highest rated debut season finale since May 2005, when Grey's Anatomy ended its first season. Empire's season one finale grew 82 percent from its series premiere, making it the show that has grown the ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire_(2015_TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d191\"},\"ref\":\"d191\",\"snippet\":\" ... On May 10, 2013, the series was renewed for a third season, which premiered on September 20, 2013, and ended on April 25, 2014, after 22 episodes.\\n\\nOn May 10, 2014, ABC renewed Last Man Standing for a fourth season, which premiered on October 3, 2014. Allen and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last_Man_Standing_(American_TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d192\"},\"ref\":\"d192\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was nominated for Favorite TV Cable Drama between 2012 and 2014. Matt Bomer won the award for Favorite TV Cable Actor in 2015. Diahann Carroll was nominated for Outstanding Supporting Actress in a Drama series at the Image Awards in 2012 and 2014. At the TV Guide ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Collar_(TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d193\"},\"ref\":\"d193\",\"snippet\":\" ... David Lynch's TV series Twin Peaks and the follow-up film Twin Peaks: Fire Walk with Me, and compared and contrasted Sud and Lynch's works.\\n\\nSeason 1\\n\\nThe series premiere was praised by most critics. Metacritic gave it a score of 84/100 based on reviews ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Killing_(American_TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d194\"},\"ref\":\"d194\",\"snippet\":\" ... The second season premiered on June 30, 2014, with King making a cameo appearance in the episode, as a customer in the Sweetbriar Rose diner. The second season ended on September 22, 2014.\\n\\nOn October 9, 2014, the series was renewed for a third season. During a CBS ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Dome_(TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d195\"},\"ref\":\"d195\",\"snippet\":\" ... The series premiered on October 8, 2014 on the Audience Network and concluded on August 2, 2017. It stars Frank Grillo, Kiele Sanchez, Matt Lauria, Jonathan Tucker, Nick Jonas, and Joanna Going. Season one consists of ten episodes.\\n\\nOn October 17, 2014, DirecTV announced that the series was ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_(American_TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d196\"},\"ref\":\"d196\",\"snippet\":\" ... premiere, and season 3 premiered on November 10, 2014, one day after the U.S. premiere. As of 2019, all episodes are available for streaming on Hotstar.\\n\\nReception\\n\\nRatings\\n\\nCritical response\\n\\nCritical reaction to the series in its first season was mixed. The show's second and third ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Newsroom_(American_TV_series)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d197\"},\"ref\":\"d197\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Time magazine's list of the \\\"100 Best TV Shows of All Time\\\" in 2007.\\n\\nAll in the Family, premiered in January 1971, is often regarded in the United States as one of the greatest television series of all time. Following a lackluster first season, the show ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sitcoms_in_the_United_States\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d198\"},\"ref\":\"d198\",\"snippet\":\" ... Hosted by Helen Mirren, the series spoofs celebrated documentary films by parodying the style of each documentary with a similar, but fictitious, subject.'Documentary Now' Is Pure, 100-Percent Film-Nerd Catnip – Rolling Stone The third season premiered on February 20, 2019. On April 8, 2019, the series ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Documentary_Now!\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d199\"},\"ref\":\"d199\",\"snippet\":\" ... The 100 was the defining show of 2014.\\n\\nWith its seventh and final season premiering in 2020, this teenage survivalist show brought the psychology of human nature to the forefront of American television. Touted as a dystopian sci-fi series set far in America's future, The 100 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.teenvogue.com/story/best-teen-tv-shows-2010s\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b1760b7a27bf1f99dc5ae94c4aaf15533f4db290a29f7a201ab1bc96c167e319\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"c99007e109da9e5cc77b2ee2e7a0418d6d7c618dcfafb88cabe4f7383496cde2\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The 100 TV series seasons premiere 2014\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_83c86181098e4e208132fe35"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":true,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d125\"},\"ref\":\"d125\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.denofgeek.com/tv/rick-and-morty-voice-actors-guide/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d138\"},\"ref\":\"d138\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Harmon\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d139\"},\"ref\":\"d139\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.tuko.co.ke/facts-lifehacks/celebrity-biographies/512328-famous-celebrities-54-inspire-dressing/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d140\"},\"ref\":\"d140\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.manhattantheatreclub.com/past-productions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d141\"},\"ref\":\"d141\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://clickamericana.com/topics/celebrities-famous-people/model-to-actor-before-they-were-famous\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d142\"},\"ref\":\"d142\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://listverse.com/2024/10/15/10-actors-who-infamously-stormed-off-set-while-filming/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d143\"},\"ref\":\"d143\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.astrotheme.com/celebrities/sun/moon/5/6.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d133\"},\"ref\":\"d133\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.sunsigns.org/january-3-famous-birthdays/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d144\"},\"ref\":\"d144\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://ew.com/tv/best-tv-theme-songs-21st-century/?srsltid=AfmBOooiefkeit4W3-Grk9msaAyUN4mDjUZ6MZvYMhGe2ByJjr6DKKtz\"}],\"next_step\":\"Open a received ref with read; use replay=true to restore full cached navigation.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":4,\"prior_deliveries\":1,\"query_key\":\"8ee75a5613f55a67a6ad4bfe44214f7e881f50b3567fa209611be755a3c03d21\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a2f7dd067cc8c9f8ca37713f48fb59b7e24ed96f6b82ac162ed262a394fe029f\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Jessica Harmon actress height\",\"view\":\"reuse\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... After all, that's the best way to make it seem like the relationship is an authentic one. In the case of Jessica and Richard Harmon, though, the siblings actually play unrelated characters in the world of The 100.\\n\\nJessica plays Niylah, a character who shows up in ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d145\"},\"ref\":\"d145\",\"snippet\":\" ... as a recurring character in the first season. She is portrayed by starring cast member Lindsey Morgan and debuts in \\\"Earth Skills\\\".\\n\\nWhile on Earth, Raven was the primary mechanic and explosives expert for the Delinquents. Raven is not part of the original the 100, however, she barters ... \",\"title\":\"https://the100.fandom.com/wiki/Raven_Reyes\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d200\"},\"ref\":\"d200\",\"snippet\":\" ... It's this focus on characters connecting and growing together that end up defining the very best romance anime series.\\n\\n35 The 100 Girlfriends Who Really, Really, Really, Really, Really Love You\\n\\nAnime series by Bibury Animation Studios; Based on the manga by Rikito Nakamura & Yukiko Nozawa\\n\\nThe ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/best-romance-anime/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d201\"},\"ref\":\"d201\",\"snippet\":\" ... But you can prove me wrong by posting a list of LGBTQ+ characters you feel are compelling and authentic.\\n\\n100% agree. How long as the hetero relationships been forced up those who are not straight? It goes both ways.\\n\\nI am so sick of the \\\"I don't ... \",\"title\":\"https://tvline.com/lists/lgbtq-representation-tv-shows-decline-glaad-report-2024/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... The most important aspect of any romance story is the central relationship between the main couple. In books, the characters' chemistry is created by the author, but in TV shows, it's up to the actors to carry the plot and convince the audience that these people are ... \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/best-romance-tv-shows-based-on-books/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d202\"},\"ref\":\"d202\",\"snippet\":\" ... Vikram Murthi from The A.V. Club also gave the episode an \\\"A\\\" rating, praising the character development and the topics covered through the series, such as contemporary relationships and living with clinical depression, and how it culminates on the series finale and in the characters choices regarding ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You%27re_the_Worst\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d203\"},\"ref\":\"d203\",\"snippet\":\" ... Hachiman and other characters are routinely forced to question how 'real' their relationships with their peers are, how much of it is guided by underlying interests, and what the purpose of these relationships is, to begin with. For anyone navigating the complexities of socializing, this anime is indispensable ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.dualshockers.com/best-anime-about-introverts/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d204\"},\"ref\":\"d204\",\"snippet\":\" ... Furthermore, a romance novel must have an \\\"emotionally satisfying and optimistic ending.\\\"\\n\\nLeslie Gelbman, a president of Berkley Books, defines the genre as stating that romance must make the \\\"romantic relationship between the hero and the heroine ... the core of the book.\\\" In general, romance novels reward characters ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance_novel\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d205\"},\"ref\":\"d205\",\"snippet\":\" ... Disney began marketing the series through soundtracks, books, dolls, toys, and video games based on Duff's character; the company reportedly made an estimated $100 million from the show's merchandise alone. The actress was featured in the Game Boy Advance video games that were created for her ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilary_Duff\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d206\"},\"ref\":\"d206\",\"snippet\":\" ... Focuses on familial relationships, conflicts, and dynamics.\\n\\n- Rebellion: Characters challenge authority or oppressive systems.\\n\\n- Time Travel: Characters move backward or forward in time, impacting the past or future.\\n\\n- Apocalypse: The story centers around a catastrophic event that threatens the survival of humanity.\\n\\n- Power and Corruption: Characters deal with ... \",\"title\":\"https://medium.com/@nathan.baugh/100-timeless-plot-archetypes-02e953f8580d\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"4a40d45f878b10c0e67efc2e7813386702e66ba64100d36ac04fad203d71925b\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b1866e4be1782856c9afd7a8cbe09ba486a260f12a80deaa418ba2650274d18c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Niylah The 100 character relationships\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_9182dcdde9cb44ff835fb165"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d15\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"30d6d8bd1feaa16d7480eae3bbb0d0772ddf0a956d9870efc705af2df5ace29e\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Screen Rant\\nauthor: Joseph Allen\\ndate: 2018-04-13\\n---\\nThe CW's slate of programming is a fascinating one. Many of its shows are actually fairly well-regarded, whether they take place inside of the network's sprawling Arrowverse or not. Part of the reason these shows have been so successful is because of their excellent casting and captivating stars.\\n\\nAlthough the CW has a number of great shows on the air and a really great talent pool, they more than occasionally like to cast actors who are actually related to one another in real life, or are married and have decided to form a new family with one another.\\n\\nWhether these two relatives show up on the same show or not depends on the specifics of the situation, but as many of the couples on this list are married, it's often the case that the two of them met while they were filming together. Other times, the relationship between the two actors was the reason that one of them was brought onto a show.\\n\\nWhatever the reasons might be, it's clear that the CW has no fears about keeping things close. After all, if one actor from a family works out, who's to say that others won't, too?\\n\\nHere are 15 CW Stars That Only True Fans Know Are Actually Family.\\n\\nStephen And Robbie Amell\\n\\nThis one is among the most readily apparent on this list, in part because Robbie and Stephen Amell share a last name. The cousins have also made homes for themselves on the CW, where they have both played superheroes.\\n\\nStephen has been Oliver Queen on Arrow for several years, and Robbie has played Firestorm on The Flash. Robbie also played a teleporting hero on Tomorrow People, which has been off the air for a few years now.\\n\\nIn addition to sharing an employer, at least sometimes, the two cousins also look quite a bit alike, and are each quite handsome. Of course, there a number of families who have spawned multiple successful actors because, at the end of the day, part of the reason actors are famous is because of their looks, which the Amells have in spades.\\n\\nJared Padalecki And Genevieve Cortese\\n\\nJared Padalecki has had a pretty long and steady career on television, and he's even had the chance to work with his future wife.\\n\\nPadalecki and Genevieve Cortese actually met on the set of Supernatural when Cortese was a recurring guest during the show's fourth season. Cortese played Ruby, a demon who seduces Padalecki's character and causes a rift to form between Sam and Dean.\\n\\nAlthough the affair between Sam and Ruby proved to be short-lived, Padalecki and Cortese's relationship turned out to be a pretty stable one. The couple eventually got married, and they now live in Austin, Texas with their three children. Supernatural is a show with plenty of tragedy, but things seemed to have ended in a happily ever after for Padalecki and Cortese.\\n\\nAly And AJ Michalka\\n\\nAly and AJ Michalka have been famous since a fairly young age. Both actresses made their debuts on the Disney Channel when they were still quite young, and they also to\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"},{\"document\":\"d15\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":9000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"07b5153b0fd4c07403bf487359b2aa985eaba53a8adb4701fd7c48991220752d\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":3000,\"text\":\"ured together as a musical act. It's safe to say that the sisters' careers have been closely related to one another, and that was also true of their work on Hellcats alongside Ashley Tisdale, another former Disney Channel star.\\n\\nThe show followed Aly's character as she used her gymnastic skills to become part of a rather fiercely competitive and drama-filled cheerleading squad. The show only lasted a single season, but that gave Aly and AJ plenty of time to be on screen with one another, and kept their sisterly bond a featured aspect of both of their careers.\\n\\nJeffrey Dean Morgan And Hillarie Burton\\n\\nJeffrey Dean Morgan has made appearances in pretty much every popular television show. Currently, he's Negan, the big bad on The Walking Dead, and in that role, he's managed to call up a lot of menace from inside him. Morgan has also made appearances on the CW in Supernatural.\\n\\nOn that show, Morgan played the role of Sam and Dean Winchester's father -- the man who inspired them to begin their life hunting demons. Morgan's wife Hillarie Burton was also a regular on the CW, playing Peyton on One Tree Hill.\\n\\nThe two have never acted on the same CW show, but both were on the network at roughly the same time.\\n\\nOf course, that was long before they were married in 2014, so maybe the CW was one of the first things they talked about.\\n\\nJessica And Richard Harmon\\n\\nActors who are siblings in real life are commonly cast to play siblings on television. After all, that's the best way to make it seem like the relationship is an authentic one. In the case of Jessica and Richard Harmon, though, the siblings actually play unrelated characters in the world of The 100.\\n\\nJessica plays Niylah, a character who shows up in the third season and has been with Clarke on a couple of different occasions. Richard played John Murphy, a recurring character during the show's first two seasons who was bumped up to a major role during the third season.\\n\\nWhatever went on behind the scenes that led both of these siblings to star on the show is unclear, but it must be nice for them both to have a friendly face on set.\\n\\nJensen Ackles And Danneel Ackles\\n\\nSupernatural is one of the longest-running shows in television history, and Jensen Ackles has been one of the show's stars for its entire run. Although Ackles's co-star Jared Padalecki met his wife on the set of Supernatural, things happened a bit differently for Ackles and his wife Danneel. Jensen and Danneel started dating in 2009 and were married in 2010, but it wasn't until 2018 that Danneel showed up on Supernatural, playing a faith healer.\\n\\nInterestingly, Danneel once tweeted that if the show made it to its 13th season, which is currently airing, that would be when she decided to guest star. It turns out, that's exactly what happened.\\n\\nIn their private life, Jensen and Danneel live in Dallas, Texas with their daughter and a pair of twins.\\n\\nKatie Cassidy And Patrick Cassidy\\n\\nYou're far more likely to know Katie Cassidy than you are her uncle, especially if you keep up with the Arrowverse shows on the CW. Katie plays Laurel Lance -- the Black Canary -- on Arrow, and has also played the role in crossover events on The Flash and Legends of Tomorrow. After Black Canary's passing, Cassidy returned to the show as an evil version of her character.\\n\\nWhile Katie Cassidy may be familiar, her uncle Patrick Cassidy is only known to CW fans because of a role he had as a non-super character on Smallville. There, he played Henry Small, Lana Lang's father, and a lawyer who had a strong hatred for the Luthor family. The relatives never overlapped on the network, but they were both there, at least for a second.\\n\\nBrandon Routh And Courtney Ford\\n\\nBrandon Routh has spent large swaths of his career playing superheroes, as he currently does on the CW's Legends of Tomorrow.\\n\\nRouth has been married to Courtney Ford for more than 10 years.\\n\\nThe couple met when Routh was a waiter, and they've been together ever since.\\n\\nRouth isn't the only one who has appeared on Legends of Tomorrow. Ford has also made appearances on the show as Nora Darhk, a character which started on Arrow before migrating over to Legends of Tomorrow. Now, Ford gets the chance to work on the same show as her husband. That might be an interesting change of pace, especially since the two of them have spent so many years working separately. Now, they see each other at home and when they get to work.\\n\\nJoseph Morgan And Persia White\\n\\nCoworkers get together all the time. It's only natural when you consider how much time they spend together, and that's doubly true of actors, who often have incredibly intense shooting schedules, and get to know one another fairly well as a result.\\n\\nThese two actors met when they were filming the third season of The Vampire Diaries. Joseph Morgan played Klaus, one of the show's original vampires, and Persia White was playing Abbie Bennett Wilson, a witch who was the mother of Bonnie Bennett.\\n\\nMorgan was eventually given his own spin-off, The Originals, and White only appeared in a handful of episodes of The Vampire Diaries, but the connection between them was enough to lead to a relationship outside of work. The two kept their relationship a secret for quite a while, but they were eventually married and have been now for over three years.\\n\\nAlexa Vega And Carlos Pena Jr.\\n\\nAlexa Vega may still be best known for her work in Spy Kids, but she was also one of the stars of The Tomorrow People, a short-lived CW show that focused on superheroes.\\n\\nVega's show may not have lasted long on the CW, but she's hopeful that her husband's project on the network will last longer.\\n\\nVega's husband Carlos Pena Jr. is currently starring in Life Sentence, a new CW show that just premiered this year. The two actors aren't on the same show, and they weren't even on the network at the same time, but it's nevertheless true that both have been employed by the CW, which feels almost like a strange coincidence.\\n\\nThere's a lot of TV out the\",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/cw-stars-family/\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\",\"e2\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":188,\"backend_calls\":92,\"model_calls\":9,\"output_reservation\":46729},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d206\"},\"ref\":\"d206\",\"snippet\":\" ... Focuses on familial relationships, conflicts, and dynamics.\\n\\n- Rebellion: Characters challenge authority or oppressive systems.\\n\\n- Time Travel: Characters \",\"title\":\"https://medium.com/@nathan.baugh/100-timeless-plot-archetypes-02e953f8580d\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d205\"},\"ref\":\"d205\",\"snippet\":\" ... Disney began marketing the series through soundtracks, books, dolls, toys, and video games based on Duff's character; the company reportedly made an estima\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilary_Duff\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d204\"},\"ref\":\"d204\",\"snippet\":\" ... Furthermore, a romance novel must have an \\\"emotionally satisfying and optimistic ending.\\\"\\n\\nLeslie Gelbman, a president of Berkley Books, defines the genre \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance_novel\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d203\"},\"ref\":\"d203\",\"snippet\":\" ... Hachiman and other characters are routinely forced to question how 'real' their relationships with their peers are, how much of it is guided by underlying \",\"title\":\"https://www.dualshockers.com/best-anime-about-introverts/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d202\"},\"ref\":\"d202\",\"snippet\":\" ... Vikram Murthi from The A.V. Club also gave the episode an \\\"A\\\" rating, praising the character development and the topics covered through the series, such as\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You%27re_the_Worst\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d201\"},\"ref\":\"d201\",\"snippet\":\" ... But you can prove me wrong by posting a list of LGBTQ+ characters you feel are compelling and authentic.\\n\\n100% agree. How long as the hetero relationships \",\"title\":\"https://tvline.com/lists/lgbtq-representation-tv-shows-decline-glaad-report-2024/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d200\"},\"ref\":\"d200\",\"snippet\":\" ... It's this focus on characters connecting and growing together that end up defining the very best romance anime series.\\n\\n35 The 100 Girlfriends Who Really, \",\"title\":\"https://screenrant.com/best-romance-anime/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d199\"},\"ref\":\"d199\",\"snippet\":\" ... The 100 was the defining show of 2014.\\n\\nWith its seventh and final season premiering in 2020, this teenage survivalist show brought the psychology of human\",\"title\":\"https://www.teenvogue.com/story/best-teen-tv-shows-2010s\"}],\"consecutive_repeat_rounds\":0,\"contract\":{\"enabled\":true,\"gap_state\":true,\"guided_read\":true,\"recovery_rounds\":2,\"repeat_threshold\":2,\"repetition\":\"bounded\",\"reuse_results\":true,\"version\":\"gap-workflow-v1\"},\"instruction\":\"Use the current missing relation to choose a real next action. Page-name search is not page reading; cached is not proof of progress.\",\"last_new_navigation_source_round\":7,\"last_new_raw_source_round\":5,\"previous_gap_judgments_not_verified\":[],\"recovery_decisions_used\":0,\"stage\":\"normal\"},\"retriever_capabilities\":{\"boolean_operators\":false,\"kind\":\"sqlite-fts5-bm25\",\"negative_result\":\"no hit for this expression is not proof that the fact is absent\",\"phrase_quotes\":false,\"query_rule\":\"lowercase; regex word extraction; first-occurrence deduplication; OR of quoted individual tokens\",\"ranking\":\"SQLite bm25(search), ascending; docid tie-break; unchanged from q26 LocalIndex\",\"scope\":\"fixed local corpus; not live web\",\"site_filter\":false,\"title_kind\":\"stored URL, not an extracted page title\",\"warning\":\"site:, quotes and AND/OR in input are not filters/operators. Their words may become ordinary search terms. Use a few discriminating terms.\"},\"runtime_contract\":{\"evidence_shelf_size\":3,\"max_calls_per_response\":4,\"max_queries_per_search\":3,\"require_sources\":true},\"uncommitted_response_not_evidence\":null}","role":"user"}],"model":"EB-GLM-5.2","temperature":0.0,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find candidate documents in the configured corpus; it does NOT open their full text.\nUSE WHEN: No suitable page is known, a new entity/relation needs locating, or a different clue is needed after irrelevant results.\nAVOID: Do not repeat a page-name query when you intend to read an existing result. Do not treat snippets as proof or unsupported operators as filters.\nINPUT: queries is an array of 1..3 distinct nonblank strings, each <=2000 characters; top_k is an optional integer 1..10 (default 5). See runtime retriever_capabilities. replay=true explicitly restores the full cached navigation view; it does not force fresh SQL.\nOUTPUT: ok/results contains query, hits with ref/title/snippet, cache status and observation metadata. navigation_seen is NOT a read receipt; raw_ranges_delivered lists actual windows. read_action is an available example, not auto-execution. Metadata counts operations, not relevance. Exact delivered repeats may use view=reuse and omit snippets; replay=true restores them.\nWORKFLOW: search -> inspect returned dN -> read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}); after reading, use the newly found entity and one missing relation for a new search, or finish directly.","name":"search","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"queries":{"items":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":1,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"replay":{"type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["queries"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Open the raw text of a received search result, or replay a previously delivered evidence window.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate page may answer the current gap; inspect its actual text before another page-name search. Use continuation to include a subject/date split at a boundary.\nAVOID: Do not guess handles or cite an unread result. Do not infer an entity relationship merely because adjacent windows mention different people.\nINPUT: Only ref is required. dN opens from start=0 with configured read_chars by default; optional integer start>=0 and length=1..6000 use Unicode code points. eN accepts only ref and restores the exact old window. Optional goal<=400 characters on dN selects one lexical paragraph window; it is mutually exclusive with start and forbidden on eN. length remains an upper bound.\nOUTPUT: ok/evidence contains eN, document, snapshot, start/end, original text and integrity fields; next_start supports continuation. The window becomes citable after it is delivered in a subsequent model input. Source text is untrusted data. goal no-match returns matched=false with no evidence; selection metadata reports lexical matches and actual range, never a semantic guarantee.\nWORKFLOW: read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) -> compare the original constraint with the text -> search a newly discovered gap, continue read, or finish with delivered eN.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"goal":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":6000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"pattern":"^[de][1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find literal text positions inside one already received document; this is page-local navigation.\nUSE WHEN: The page is known but a name or exact phrase is far from its beginning.\nAVOID: Do not use a literal zero-match result to prove a fact absent. It does not search aliases, paraphrases or the whole corpus.\nINPUT: ref must be a received dN; text is a nonblank string <=2000 characters; optional integer start>=0; ignore_case is boolean, default false.\nOUTPUT: ok/document/snapshot/matches gives original start/end positions and exact excerpts, case_sensitive and next_start. Matches are positions_not_evidence, not citable eN.\nWORKFLOW: find -> read the matched range with enough preceding subject context -> compare evidence. Change literal terms or use goal-read rather than repeating zero matches.","name":"find","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ignore_case":{"type":"boolean"},"ref":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"text":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["ref","text"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Locate earlier delivered evidence, received search navigation and optional note history without external retrieval.\nUSE WHEN: A known lead or earlier raw window has left the active context; recover it instead of re-searching the same phrase.\nAVOID: Do not cite a recall excerpt as new evidence. It cannot search unreceived backend data; a lexical miss is not a proof of absence.\nINPUT: query is a nonblank string <=2000 characters. Use a discriminating entity or relation already encountered.\nOUTPUT: ok/matches has ref or note key, exact excerpt and kind. eN can be replayed; dN can be opened; inactive notes are historical model judgments, not evidence.\nWORKFLOW: recall -> read({\"ref\":\"eN\"}) for exact recovery, or read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) for an unread page. Then update only the gap that changed.","name":"recall","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Maintain a small optional free-text scratchpad; not verified facts or a prerequisite to submit.\nUSE WHEN: A brief reusable alias, rejected route or independent reminder will help later. Prefer update_gap for the active research question when available.\nAVOID: Do not summarize every page, copy the full question, or repeatedly write the same note. Notes do not automatically retract dependent plans.\nINPUT: put requires op/key/text/anchors; text <=600 characters, anchors is <=6 delivered eN. delete requires op/key only. Keys are 1..32 ASCII letters/digits/_/-. Capacity is explicit.\nOUTPUT: ok/key/changed and kind=agent_note_not_evidence, or deleted. A no-op is not research progress. Errors do not silently alter saved notes.\nWORKFLOW: Optionally save a useful observation alongside another already-planned action; keep sources in the archive and finish without cleanup.","name":"notes","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchors":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"put"},"text":{"maxLength":600,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["op","key","text","anchors"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"delete"}},"required":["op","key"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Explicitly submit the requested answer with source windows, or explicitly abstain.\nUSE WHEN: The requested core answer has sufficient support, or the available budget/evidence cannot resolve it. No note, gap update or audit is mandatory.\nAVOID: Do not claim every clue is verified when it is not. Do not change established into expanded, by-year into in-year, or hide unresolved numeric conflicts in a long explanation.\nINPUT: Answer branch requires answer and refs. Nonblank strings are <=8000 characters; string-integer-v1 additionally permits plain JSON integers, not bools/floats, rendered as decimal text. Strings stay exact. Abstention requires abstain=true and nonblank reason<=2000 characters. Never mix branches. refs contains only delivered eN, <=16; configured source and literal-format requirements still apply.\nOUTPUT: ok/terminal records submitted or abstained. Submitted answer is text with refs/basis and any representation metadata. Legal references are NOT semantic verification. Explicit prefix/suffix constraints still apply.\nWORKFLOW: Finish last in a response, based only on evidence already received for that decision. Never combine a new read and a guessed citation to its unseen result. In FINAL only finish is allowed.","name":"finish","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"answer":{"maxLength":8000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":["string","integer"]},"refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true}},"required":["answer","refs"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"abstain":{"const":true},"reason":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["abstain","reason"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Replace the one active research question and retain a bounded history of explicit model judgments; it is NOT an automatic verifier.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate, unresolved relation, rejection or conflict changed, or repeated searches need a concrete next objective. Use sparingly, not after every tool.\nAVOID: Do not turn the original question or your prior guess into evidence. Updating a gap does not count as a new observation and does not reset a search loop.\nINPUT: subject/question/basis are nonblank <=400 characters; kind and status follow schema; evidence_refs are <=6 received eN, navigation_refs <=6 received dN; next_action is one named existing tool. supported/rejected/conflict require evidence_refs. Supply a concise decision basis, not a transcript.\nOUTPUT: ok/changed/current returns agent_judgment_not_verified with revision. At most four previous distinct gap versions remain in the active view; the full update is journaled. Sources are checked for delivery, not entailment.\nWORKFLOW: Observe -> identify one missing relationship or record a real rejection -> select read on an available page or search for a new relation. An update may share a response with known independent actions; no update is required before finish.","name":"update_gap","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"evidence_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"kind":{"enum":["locate","read","relation","disambiguate","conflict","recover"]},"navigation_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"next_action":{"enum":["search","read","find","recall","finish"]},"question":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["open","supported","rejected","conflict"]},"subject":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["subject","question","kind","status","evidence_refs","navigation_refs","next_action","basis"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}]}